<title>USA: SGL Carbon says records subpoenaed.</title>
<headline>SGL Carbon says records subpoenaed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>SGL Carbon AG said on Thursday that antitrust authorities of the European Community and the United States have issued search warrants for certain company documents.</p>
<p>The company said it believes the search is related to investigations into alleged price fixing among graphite electrode manufacturers.</p>
<p>Earlier Thursday, trading in the company's U.S. shares was suspended and its shares had fallen 4-3/4 to 46 before the halt.</p>
<p>SGL Carbon's rival, UCAR International Inc, said it also had been served with a subpoena and related search warrant from a U.S. grand jury investigating alleged price fixing in the industry.</p>
<p>&quot;SGL Carbon is producing the documents sought by the investigators,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
